From: EglantinePS5
Subject: up: EDEN_NX2_SKIP_SAME read once per 3D engine into a member (unconditional, behaviour-neutral)

What: Maxwell3D::SkipSameValueWrites() was a static function with a function-local static, called
on every state register write (CallMethod, MacroWrite's short path) and every sink run, so each call
checked the static's guard. It is now a member function returning a const member that the engine
sets when it is made; the old static (renamed SkipSameValueWritesFirst) is only its initializer.
Callers unchanged (all in maxwell_3d.cpp, all members).

No switch, behaviour-neutral: the member takes the old static's value, so it is the value of the
process's first read, as before. The only change is that the first read happens when the first 3D
engine is made instead of at its first method write. Nothing sets EDEN_NX2_SKIP_SAME between the
two: the front applies the testing switches, env.txt and env-<title id>.txt in main before the game
loads (headless/main.cpp), and no core or front code sets that name later (setenv only in
headless/main.cpp, memory_check.cpp and freedreno_debug.cpp, none of them for it).
Not taken: the EDEN_NX2_PERF_VERIFY half (Nx2Perf::Verify()). Our core has no Nx2Perf / CallMethodFast
path, so there is nothing to move. Nothing to see in a log (a few instructions per write).

Origin and credit: the missing part of zortos293/Lichii 794602bfbd (#778), Zortos, from Frizti's
Fritchii v4 and Marc Stampfli's #488 (its profile: the SKIP_SAME guard check was 0.9% of the back
thread on a PC, the PERF_VERIFY one 0.3%).
